        "In Saudi Arabia, the Saudi Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest Registry (SOHAR) reported 3,671 OHCAs between 2019 and 2022; 82.6% occurred at home, prehospital return of spontaneous circulation was 7.4%, and survival to hospital discharge was only 2.9% [2]. These figures indicate a large potential benefit from strengthening the community links of the chain of survival.",
        "Locally, a 2023 cross-sectional survey of adults in the Al-Majma'ah region documented gaps in basic life support (BLS) awareness, particularly regarding the correct initial steps when encountering a collapsed person, and many participants reported discomfort performing hands-only CPR because of limited knowledge and skills [3]. This establishes the local need; the next logical question is whether a feasible intervention can change performance.",
