        "Saudi Arabia's hot climate exposes outdoor workers (construction, agriculture, cleaning, delivery and security workers) to substantial occupational heat stress. Saudi heat research has concentrated largely on Hajj pilgrims. A 2023 study of military personnel in Jeddah found generally good knowledge but gaps in practices, such as receiving medical briefings and guidance on treatment [2], and noted that earlier Saudi heat-knowledge research had focused on pilgrims and the general population rather than outdoor workers.",
