        "A national survey of 805 adults conducted during the COVID-19 period reported that 66% were aware of the EMS phone number; ambulances arrived within 8 minutes in 53.6% of 997 calls versus 35.5% of Asefny requests [1]. An earlier comparative study of SRCA data found no significant difference in response phases between the application and phone requests [2]. In stroke, not arriving by ambulance and living outside Riyadh city were associated with late hospital arrival [5].",
        "Underuse of EMS may also contribute to Saudi OHCA outcomes, where most arrests occur at home and survival remains low [3]. Improving digital and prehospital services is consistent with Vision 2030 health transformation objectives [4].",
