    gap="Existing Saudi studies were conducted during the COVID-19 lockdown or analysed administrative request data [1, 2]. The search for this portfolio did not identify a post-pandemic national study comparing urban and rural populations on awareness of 997, awareness and use of Asefny, intended EMS use for specific emergencies (e.g., stroke, chest pain, collapse), and barriers to calling. This is a <b>national gap</b> with a specific <b>urban-rural</b> dimension relevant to Majmaah.",
    gap_type="National (literature-supported)",
    question="Among adults living in Saudi Arabia (P), is rural residence (E) compared with urban residence (C) associated with lower awareness of the 997 number and the Asefny application and lower intended EMS use for time-critical emergencies (O)?",
