        "In Saudi Arabia, several single-centre studies have reported high proportions of non-urgent ED visits. A study in a tertiary centre in western Saudi Arabia found that 78.5% of non-life-threatening visits were non-urgent (Canadian Triage and Acuity Scale levels IV-V); the commonest reasons were perceived urgency (42.0%), easy access (25.5%) and limited primary healthcare resources (17.8%) [3]. An earlier study also examined reasons for non-urgent presentations in Saudi Arabia [4].",
